<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-chapter-Basic-Probability" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Basic Probability Concepts and Combinatorics</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> The problem sets provided here will give you practice with the fundamentals ideas of classical probability theory, such as probability experiments, sample spaces, and the use of counting techniques. </p>

      <p> Each problem set contains two types of problems: interactive exercises and non-interactive ("written") exercises. You will be able to check your answers and get immediate feedback on the interactive portion.
      </p>

      <p> Note: This is a work in progress. These problems sets are still being edited and solutions checked for accuracy and clarity.
      </p>
  </introduction>

